"2D game character attack animation, full body, front view. Make every motion big, bold and exaggerated, with strong clear poses that read instantly even on a tiny phone screen. A young warlord with long black hair, a red headband, red and gold armor and a long red cape stands facing the viewer; his right hand holds a tall halberd upright beside him, its butt on the ground and its curved blade with a red tassel at the height of his head; his left hand rests on his hip. Wind-up, the first third of a second: he grips the halberd short with both hands, shifts his weight onto his back leg and tilts the shaft so that the curved blade swings down from beside his head to chest height in front of him, never over or behind his back. Release: he steps his front foot forward, bends the knee deep and drives the blade diagonally down across his body until its point is near the ground at his other side; red fire runs along the edge of the blade and fades. Recovery, the rest of the clip: he straightens, stands the halberd upright in his right hand and settles into exactly the same pose as the first frame. The blade of the halberd never rises higher than at the start. He moves like a living man, with natural weight shifts, bending knees and a supple spine; he never rotates rigidly like a figurine on a stand. He always faces the viewer and never shows his back. He never moves toward or away from the camera and his size in the frame stays the same. His whole body and the halberd stay inside the frame at all times. His body stays solid and fully visible in every frame. Static locked-off camera: no zoom, no pan, no shake. Keep the character design exactly identical in every frame. Plain flat solid gray background exactly as in the input image, unchanged for the whole video: no floor, no shadow, no smoke, no dust. Smooth, weighty, high-quality game animation; the last frame matches the first frame."
